e scenario, `not-found-tab-reads-the-shop-name`, is the happy path, so it gets a Playwright test. It also checks that the parts of the page that don't change are still there.\n- **Changed tests:** none. The only committed not-found test, `ShopFlowTest.UnknownPageRendersThe404Page`, checks the 404 status and the error code, and both still hold.\n- **Context finding:** the story names `portal`, and Portal is on both maps, which agree. But the page is actually rendered by `ErrorPageController` in the web host, not by the Portal project. The plan changes the view where it is and moves nothing.\n- **How the URL gets there:** `/products/no-such-product` doesn't match the product page's `{productId:guid}` route. The shop's status-code handling then shows the 404 page. No Product code changes.\n- **Open assumptions:** I didn't check that the Java sample's page has the same title. The new test's title also has to be added to the shared scenario list, but that check only runs when the shared specification is passed in (`-p:SpecificationPath=…`); otherwise it is skipped. Neither was an input to this stage.\n- **No `needs-human`**, so the run is not stopped.\n\n**Before you continue:** the working tree shows this story already went through every stage and the acceptance record (`not-found-title-accept-1`) says `accepted`. The view change and the new tests are already there, uncommitted. My plan replaced the earlier, untracked `plan.md` without my reading it first, because the skill says to plan without looking at an earlier run. The status hook also says a worker (`runner:zuse.local:51363`) holds this checkout with the story marked as running. I didn't run any other stage.","ttft_ms":2934,"type":"result","duration_ms":74014,"uuid":"f3033051-b651-4edd-8c02-c2d74ef164aa","ttft_stream_ms":1736,"time_to_request_ms":65,"first_content_frame_ms":1737,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
